 "readme": {
  "overview": "VirtoCommerce.ModuleFederation scans installed .NET module manifests for `<frontendModules>` declarations, resolves which modules belong to which host apps via the dependency graph, and serves a runtime API that host apps use to load remote MF bundles. **Key properties:** - Modules are host-agnostic — they declare capabilities, not consumers - .NET dependency graph provides intelligent defaults (Recommended modules) - All other compatible modules are visible as Available for manual activation - Admin has final control over which modules are enabled per app - Installing a .NET module auto-enables its frontend extensions for related apps",
